{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Checking Kubernetes settings does not necessarily require changing them. Incident investigation or deployment checks often need only current values."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I gave a developer ConfigMap read access in QueryPie Community and blocked modifications. Browser reads worked, Apply was denied by policy, and both attempts were auditable."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Registering a Lab Kubernetes Cluster"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I registered a separate Mac cluster as acp-kac-lab and created ConfigMap kac-fixture in namespace orders-lab, simulating order-service settings. ConfigMaps store application configuration values."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I entered API address and credentials, clicked Verify Credential, confirmed Verified, and saved with Request Audit enabled."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubernetes-policies/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Cluster credentials verified and registered in QueryPie.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Cluster credentials verified and registered in QueryPie."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Creating a Role for Configuration Inspection"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Orders Lab ConfigMap Read Only permits get/list/watch on ConfigMaps in orders-lab and denies patch/update on kac-fixture. Cluster, resource type, and operations can be specified separately."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubernetes-policies/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Policy specifies namespace, resource type, and permitted operations.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Policy specifies namespace, resource type, and permitted operations."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I attached it to Orders Lab Viewer and assigned Demo Developer. Role assignment also exposes an expiration date. Bundling task privileges in one role was convenient."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubernetes-policies/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Demo Developer assigned the configuration-viewing role.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Demo Developer assigned the configuration-viewing role."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Opening Configuration as the Developer"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Demo Developer selected Orders Lab Viewer in Kubernetes and clicked Connect, opening Web Client in the browser."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In Config & Storage → ConfigMap, orders-lab listed kac-fixture. Its YAML showed status READY."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubernetes-policies/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Developer listing ConfigMaps in orders-lab.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Developer listing ConfigMaps in orders-lab."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The user could read necessary settings without cluster-wide administration. Operators define boundaries; users choose a role and inspect permitted information."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Attempting to Change the Same Setting"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Edit changed status from READY to QUERYPIE_CHANGE_TEST. View Diff compared the single line before and after, clarifying the intended change before Apply."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubernetes-policies/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. Changing one test value and inspecting the diff.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. Changing one test value and inspecting the diff."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Apply returned ‘QueryPie - Denied by policy to access the resource.’ Reads were allowed, but the modification was denied by QueryPie policy."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubernetes-policies/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. Policy blocks the configuration change.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. Policy blocks the configuration change."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After closing and refreshing, status was still READY and resource version unchanged. Reads continued, but the unauthorized change never applied."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The underlying Kubernetes permissions allowed this change in the lab. QueryPie’s read-only policy added the denial, demonstrating task-specific control on top of Kubernetes privileges."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Auditing Who Attempted Which Change"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Audit → Kubernetes → Request Audit contained the reads and modification. Details identified Demo Developer, Orders Lab Viewer, acp-kac-lab, and orders-lab/kac-fixture."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Verb was update and Event Type DENY. The message explained policy denial, and Request Body retained QUERYPIE_CHANGE_TEST."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubernetes-policies/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. User, role, resource, operation, and denial reason.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. User, role, resource, operation, and denial reason."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The administrator could inspect the attempted work, not just the fact of a block, before asking the user for an explanation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Separating Reads from Changes in Operations"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The read after the failed change was get, Success, Event Type ALLOW, Request Source Web Client. The Kubernetes group qp-kac-demo was also visible."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubernetes-policies/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. Reads after the attempted change succeed and remain audited.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. Reads after the attempted change succeed and remain audited."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "‘Inspect settings without delegating changes’ can be expressed as policy and role. Users read in the browser; administrators control modifications and inspect requests."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This extended the same management pattern from databases and servers to Kubernetes. A unified view of users, privileges, and activity across resources should help evaluators."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This lab used QueryPie Community 11.6.7 Web Client (Beta), a separate cluster, and a ConfigMap containing only test values."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
